         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nTo understand the long division algorithm, it is essential to know multiplication well. Before continuing, we recommend studying all the texts about multiplication in the *First steps (Volume 1)* section:\n\n- **Adding the same numbers**: shows that multiplying is a way of adding the same number several times (<htcite0>)\n- **The result is (Phase II)**: presents the names of the terms of a multiplication and of its result (<htcite1>)\n- **Inversion**: explores the inverse relationship between multiplication and division (<htcite2>)\n- **Yupana (multiplication)**: teaches how to multiply with the Inca yupana (<htcite3>)\n- **Multiplying with Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты)**: presents multiplication on these abacuses (<htcite4>)\n- **Drawing the multiplication**: shows how to represent a multiplication with drawings (<htcite5>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Table (0 and 1)**: studies the multiplication tables of 0 and 1 (<htcite6>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Table (2 and 3)**: studies the multiplication tables of 2 and 3 (<htcite7>)\n- **Multiplying with the body (Level 1)**: practices multiplication using the body, level 1 (<htcite8>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Table (4 and 5)**: studies the multiplication tables of 4 and 5 (<htcite9>)\n- **Multiplying with the body (Level 2)**: practices multiplication using the body, level 2 (<htcite10>)\n- **Learning from nature**: observes multiplication patterns present in nature (<htcite11>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Table (6 and 7)**: studies the multiplication tables of 6 and 7 (<htcite12>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Table (8 and 9)**: studies the multiplication tables of 8 and 9 (<htcite13>)\n- **Understanding the Multiplication Tables (Summary)**: summarizes all the multiplication tables (<htcite14>)\n- **Multiplying the Findings**: applies the multiplication tables to what has been discovered (<htcite15>)\n- **Reading and Multiplying**: shows multiplication while reading a text (<htcite16>)\n- **Rereading**: revisits multiplication through rereading (<htcite17>)\n- **Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты) in rereading**: uses these abacuses while rereading (<htcite18>)\n- **Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты): multiplication in practice**: practices multiplication on these abacuses (<htcite19>)\n- **Our Week**: uses the seven days of the week in multiplication (<htcite20>)\n- **Practicing multiplication with Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты)**: offers an application to practice multiplication (<htcite21>)\n- **Multiplying without barriers with Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты)**: goes further in practicing multiplication on these abacuses (<htcite22>)\n- **Mesoamerican calendars**: relates multiplication to Mesoamerican calendars (<htcite23>)\n- **Mesoamerican sums**: presents sums and multiplication in Mesoamerican records (<htcite24>)\n- **Mesoamerican Multiplication**: multiplies with Mesoamerican numerals (<htcite25>)\n- **Ages and Pyramids**: applies multiplication to ages and pyramids (<htcite26>)",
